---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import CaseHeader from '../../components/CaseHeader.astro';
import Turn from '../../components/Turn.astro';
import { project, views } from '@portfolio/content';
const p = project('hdmi-dvi-transmitter');
---
<Base
  title={views.caseTitle(p)}
  description={p.description}
  kind="work-case"
  depth={1}
  ground={p.ground}
>
<main id="main">

  <CaseHeader project={p}>
    <figure class="fig fig--bleed" id="fig-1">
      <div class="fig__scroll" tabindex="0" role="group" aria-labelledby="fig-1-cap">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 800 120" preserveAspectRatio="xMinYMin meet" role="img" aria-labelledby="f1t">
          <title id="f1t">One horizontal line of 640 by 480 video timing, drawn to scale: de is high for 640 clocks and low for 160; hsync is low from clock 656 to 751 inside the 800-clock line.</title>
          <g class="s-axis" stroke-dasharray="2 3"><path d="M640 16 V104"/><path d="M656 16 V104"/><path d="M752 16 V104"/></g>
          <path class="crisp" d="M0 28 H640 V48 H800"/>
          <path class="crisp s-ramp" d="M0 76 H656 V96 H752 V76 H800"/>
          <text class="t-ink" x="4" y="22">de</text>
          <text class="t-ink" x="4" y="70">hsync</text>
          <text x="320" y="116" text-anchor="middle">active 640</text>
          <text x="648" y="116" text-anchor="middle">16</text>
          <text x="704" y="116" text-anchor="middle">sync 96</text>
          <text x="776" y="116" text-anchor="middle">48</text>
        </svg>
      </div>
      <figcaption id="fig-1-cap"><span class="fig__no">Fig.&nbsp;1</span> — One line of 640×480 @ 25.175 MHz: 640 active, 16 front porch, 96 sync, 48 back porch; 800 clocks in all. Drawn to scale; hsync low from clock 656 to 751.</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </CaseHeader>

  <section class="page">
    <div class="prose-block col-full">

      <h2 class="col-head" id="four-stages">Four stages</h2>
      <aside class="note col-margin">25.175 MHz pixel clock · 800×525 total</aside>
      <p class="col-prose">The transmitter is a DVI video pipeline for the HDMI connector on a PYNQ-Z2, written from scratch in Verilog and started in July 2026 — plain DVI, with no audio and no data islands: three TMDS channels and a clock. It has four stages: a parameterized video timing generator, a pattern generator, a TMDS <span class="mono">8b/10b</span> encoder, and a <span class="nb">10:1</span> serializer driving differential outputs. The first three exist and pass their testbenches; the serializer’s port list exists, and its body is still being written.</p>
      <p class="col-prose">The timing generator is parameterized on the eight standard numbers and derives the rest as localparams. It produces <span class="nb">640×480</span> active pixels inside an <span class="nb">800×525</span> total frame — <span class="nb">16</span> front porch, <span class="nb">96</span> sync and <span class="nb">48</span> back porch clocks on every line; <span class="nb">10</span>, <span class="nb">2</span> and <span class="nb">33</span> lines around every frame — at a <span class="nb">25.175 MHz</span> pixel clock, and outputs hsync, vsync, de and 12-bit x/y counters. The pattern generator is deliberately simple for now: a horizontal red ramp, <span class="mono">red = x mod 256</span>, green and blue zero, black outside de.</p>

      <h2 class="col-head" id="encoder">The encoder</h2>
      <p class="col-prose">TMDS encoding is done in two stages, kept separate in the RTL so each can be reasoned about alone. The first counts the ones in the byte and chooses XOR or XNOR chaining to minimize transitions, flagging the choice in <span class="mono">bit 8</span>. The second is a DC-balance stage: it keeps a signed running disparity, <span class="mono">cnt_r</span>, and decides whether to invert the eight data bits to pull it back toward zero, flagging that in <span class="mono">bit 9</span>.</p>
      <p class="col-prose">During blanking the encoder ignores the data, emits one of the four DVI control codewords selected by <span class="mono">c0</span>/<span class="mono">c1</span> (Fig.&nbsp;2), and resets the disparity to zero. The disparity arithmetic is where I expected mistakes, so that is where the testbench looks hardest.</p>

      <figure class="fig fig--right" id="fig-2">
        <div class="fig__scroll" tabindex="0" role="group" aria-labelledby="fig-2-cap">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 800 176" role="img" aria-labelledby="f2t">
            <title id="f2t">The four DVI control codewords as stepped waveforms, drawn in transmission order with q[0] first: c1c0 = 00, 01, 10 and 11, each written beside its waveform as q[9:0].</title>
            <text x="130" y="14">transmitted q[0] → q[9]</text>
            <text x="520" y="14">q[9:0] as written</text>

            <text class="t-ink" x="0" y="44">c1c0 = 00</text>
            <path class="s-rule" d="M130 49 V53 M166 49 V53 M202 49 V53 M238 49 V53 M274 49 V53 M310 49 V53 M346 49 V53 M382 49 V53 M418 49 V53 M454 49 V53 M490 49 V53"/>
            <path class="crisp" d="M130 49 H202 V29 H238 V49 H274 V29 H310 V49 H346 V29 H382 V49 H418 V29 H490"/>
            <text class="t-ink" x="520" y="44">1101010100</text>

            <text class="t-ink" x="0" y="82">c1c0 = 01</text>
            <path class="s-rule" d="M130 87 V91 M166 87 V91 M202 87 V91 M238 87 V91 M274 87 V91 M310 87 V91 M346 87 V91 M382 87 V91 M418 87 V91 M454 87 V91 M490 87 V91"/>
            <path class="crisp" d="M130 67 H202 V87 H238 V67 H274 V87 H310 V67 H346 V87 H382 V67 H418 V87 H490"/>
            <text class="t-ink" x="520" y="82">0010101011</text>

            <text class="t-ink" x="0" y="120">c1c0 = 10</text>
            <path class="s-rule" d="M130 125 V129 M166 125 V129 M202 125 V129 M238 125 V129 M274 125 V129 M310 125 V129 M346 125 V129 M382 125 V129 M418 125 V129 M454 125 V129 M490 125 V129"/>
            <path class="crisp" d="M130 125 H202 V105 H238 V125 H274 V105 H310 V125 H346 V105 H382 V125 H418 V105 H454 V125 H490"/>
            <text class="t-ink" x="520" y="120">0101010100</text>

            <text class="t-ink" x="0" y="158">c1c0 = 11</text>
            <path class="s-rule" d="M130 163 V167 M166 163 V167 M202 163 V167 M238 163 V167 M274 163 V167 M310 163 V167 M346 163 V167 M382 163 V167 M418 163 V167 M454 163 V167 M490 163 V167"/>
            <path class="crisp" d="M130 143 H202 V163 H238 V143 H274 V163 H310 V143 H346 V163 H382 V143 H418 V163 H454 V143 H490"/>
            <text class="t-ink" x="520" y="158">1010101011</text>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <figcaption id="fig-2-cap"><span class="fig__no">Fig.&nbsp;2</span> — The four control codewords the encoder emits during blanking, drawn q[0] first as transmitted; written q[9:0] as in the DVI 1.0 spec. Checked against the spec by the testbench.</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <h2 class="col-head" id="try">Try the encoder</h2>
      <p class="col-prose">Fig.&nbsp;3 is the encoder itself, ported line for line from the RTL to JavaScript so it can be driven from the page. Pick a byte and the figure shows what each stage does with it: the ones count and the XOR or XNOR choice, the nine-bit <span class="mono">q_m</span>, the DC-balance decision with the reason the RTL used, and the ten bits that leave the encoder, drawn <span class="mono">q[0]</span> first as in Fig.&nbsp;2. Set a prior disparity to reach the inversion branch, or feed the ramp to watch <span class="mono">cnt_r</span> accumulate over a video line the way it does for the red-ramp pattern, reset to zero in blanking. Under the figure is a self-check that runs in the reader’s browser every time this page loads: all <span class="nb">256</span> bytes through the encoder and back through a decoder written from the testbench’s, with the transition count and the disparity bound checked over one full line.</p>

      <figure class="fig fig--bleed" id="fig-tmds">
        <div class="tmds__ctl">
          <label>d = <span id="tmds-d">0x47</span><input id="tmds-in" type="range" min="0" max="255" value="71" disabled></label>
          <label>prior cnt_r = <span id="tmds-c">0</span><input id="tmds-cnt" type="range" min="-8" max="8" step="2" value="0" disabled></label>
          <label><input id="tmds-run" type="checkbox" disabled>feed the ramp</label>
          <output id="tmds-out" for="tmds-in tmds-cnt" class="tmds__check"><span id="tmds-res">q_out = 0100111101 · cnt_r 0 → +2</span><span class="tmds__why" id="tmds-why">N1 = 4 ones in d, d[0] = 1 → XOR chain, q_m[8] = 1
q_m[7:0]: 5 ones, 3 zeros · cnt_r = 0 → q_m[8] decides → keep, q_out[9] = 0</span></output>
        </div>
        <div class="fig__scroll" tabindex="0" role="group" aria-labelledby="fig-tmds-cap">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 800 320" role="img" aria-labelledby="ftt">
            <title id="ftt">The TMDS encoder on one byte: the input bits, the nine-bit q_m after the transition-minimizing stage, and the ten-bit q_out after DC balancing, each drawn as a stepped waveform bit 0 first and written beside it msb first, with the ones count, the chaining choice, the inversion decision and the running disparity before and after. Below, the running disparity as a stepped trace, plus or minus 8 full scale, against the input byte d, 0x00 to 0xFF.</title>
            <text x="130" y="11">bit 0 first, as transmitted</text>
            <text x="520" y="11">written msb first</text>

            <text class="t-ink" id="tl-d" x="0" y="38">d = 0x47</text>
            <path class="s-rule" d="M130 43 V47 M166 43 V47 M202 43 V47 M238 43 V47 M274 43 V47 M310 43 V47 M346 43 V47 M382 43 V47 M418 43 V47"/>
            <path class="crisp" id="tw-d" d="M130 23 H238 V43 H346 V23 H382 V43 H418"/>
            <text class="t-ink" id="ts-d" x="520" y="38">01000111</text>
            <text class="t-ink" id="tn-d" x="620" y="38">N1 = 4</text>

            <text class="t-ink" x="0" y="76">q_m</text>
            <path class="s-rule" d="M130 81 V85 M166 81 V85 M202 81 V85 M238 81 V85 M274 81 V85 M310 81 V85 M346 81 V85 M382 81 V85 M418 81 V85 M454 81 V85"/>
            <path class="crisp" id="tw-m" d="M130 61 H166 V81 H202 V61 H346 V81 H418 V61 H454"/>
            <text class="t-ink" id="ts-m" x="520" y="76">100111101</text>
            <text class="t-ink" id="tn-m" x="620" y="76">XOR · q_m[8] = 1</text>

            <text class="t-ink" x="0" y="114">q_out</text>
            <path class="s-rule" d="M130 119 V123 M166 119 V123 M202 119 V123 M238 119 V123 M274 119 V123 M310 119 V123 M346 119 V123 M382 119 V123 M418 119 V123 M454 119 V123 M490 119 V123"/>
            <path class="crisp" id="tw-q" d="M130 99 H166 V119 H202 V99 H346 V119 H418 V99 H454 V119 H490"/>
            <text class="t-ink" id="ts-q" x="520" y="114">0100111101</text>
            <text class="t-ink" id="tn-q" x="620" y="114">cnt_r 0 → +2</text>

            <text class="t-ink" id="tx-1" x="0" y="141">N1 = 4 ones in d, d[0] = 1 → XOR chain, q_m[8] = 1</text>
            <text class="t-ink" id="tx-2" x="0" y="157">q_m[7:0]: 5 ones, 3 zeros · cnt_r = 0 → q_m[8] decides → keep, q_out[9] = 0</text>

            <g transform="translate(0 122)">
              <path class="s-axis" d="M0 110 H768 M764 46 H768 M764 174 H768"/>
              <polyline class="crisp s-ramp" id="tmds-trace" points="183,110 213,110 213,94 246,94"/>
              <path class="s-axis" d="M1.5 178 V182 M193.5 178 V182 M385.5 178 V182 M577.5 178 V182 M766.5 178 V182"/>
              <text x="0" y="196">0x00</text>
              <text x="193.5" y="196" text-anchor="middle">0x40</text>
              <text x="385.5" y="196" text-anchor="middle">0x80</text>
              <text x="577.5" y="196" text-anchor="middle">0xC0</text>
              <text x="766.5" y="196" text-anchor="end">0xFF</text>
              <text x="780" y="196">d</text>
              <text x="772" y="50">+8</text>
              <text x="772" y="114">0</text>
              <text x="772" y="178">−8</text>
            </g>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <p class="tmds__check" id="tmds-check">self-check: not run — this line needs JavaScript</p>
        <figcaption id="fig-tmds-cap"><span class="fig__no">Fig.&nbsp;3</span> — The encoder, ported from the RTL: the input byte, q_m after the transition stage and q_out after DC balancing, drawn q[0] first as transmitted, written msb first. Below, the running disparity cnt_r at ±8 full scale against the input byte d: at rest, the first 256-symbol pass of the ramp from cnt_r = 0; after a slider moves, this one symbol before and after, drawn at its byte.</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <aside class="pull">
        <p class="pull__kicker">verification</p>
        <p><span class="mono">decode(encode(d)) == d</span>, on every symbol, against a decoder written independently.</p>
      </aside>

      <h2 class="col-head" id="testbenches">What the testbenches check</h2>
      <aside class="note col-margin">10,816 data symbols per run · 4 properties each</aside>
      <p class="col-prose">The encoder has a self-checking XSIM testbench that checks four properties on every symbol: round trip — <span class="mono">decode(encode(d)) == d</span> against an independently written decoder; at most five transitions per data symbol; an independently accumulated running disparity, kept from the ten transmitted bits, that matches the encoder’s own <span class="mono">cnt_r</span> every cycle; and a bounded <span class="mono">|disparity|</span>, with the bench’s limit at <span class="nb">12</span>. Control periods are checked against the four spec codewords. One run covers <span class="nb">10,816</span> data symbols: every byte value ascending and descending, each value held for eight cycles to provoke disparity drift, long runs of four constants, and forty random bursts with blanking between them.</p>
      <p class="col-prose">A second testbench drives the timing generator and the pattern generator together, waits for de at <span class="mono">x = 0, y = 0</span>, and dumps the full <span class="nb">640×480</span> frame from simulation to a PPM file so it can be checked numerically rather than by eye. Alongside it, it checks seven timing counts against constants: active pixels per frame, active lines, hsync pulses, total hsync and vsync cycles, and the length of every de run and every hsync pulse. Fig.&nbsp;4 is that frame, placed inside the <span class="nb">800×525</span> timing envelope it was generated in.</p>

      <figure class="fig fig--bleed plate" id="fig-4">
        <div class="envelope">
          <img src="../assets/hdmi-frame-640x480.png" width="640" height="480" loading="eager" alt="Simulated 640 by 480 frame: three horizontal red ramps from black to red, repeating every 256 pixels.">
          <p class="envelope__lbl envelope__lbl--right">blanking 160</p>
          <p class="envelope__lbl envelope__lbl--bottom">blanking 45 lines<span class="envelope__x"> (10 / 2 / 33)</span></p>
        </div>
        <div class="scale" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg class="scale__bar" viewBox="0 0 800 28" preserveAspectRatio="none" aria-hidden="true">
            <line x1="0" y1="8" x2="800" y2="8"/>
            <line x1="0" y1="0" x2="0" y2="8"/>
            <line class="s-cu" x1="256" y1="0" x2="256" y2="8"/>
            <line class="s-cu" x1="512" y1="0" x2="512" y2="8"/>
            <line x1="640" y1="0" x2="640" y2="8"/>
            <line x1="800" y1="0" x2="800" y2="8"/>
          </svg>
          <span class="scale__lbl scale__lbl--0">0</span>
          <span class="scale__lbl scale__lbl--256">256</span>
          <span class="scale__lbl scale__lbl--512">512</span>
          <span class="scale__lbl scale__lbl--640">640</span>
          <span class="scale__lbl scale__lbl--800">800</span>
        </div>
        <figcaption><span class="fig__no">Fig.&nbsp;4</span> — The frame the timing/pattern testbench dumped from XSIM to PPM, placed inside the 800×525 frame it was generated in; red is x mod 256. Seven timing counts checked against constants.</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <p class="col-prose">Fig.&nbsp;5 lays the pipeline out with its coverage. The frame testbench brackets the first two stages, the encoder testbench the third, and the serializer is drawn dashed because its body is not yet written.</p>

      <figure class="fig fig--right" id="fig-5">
        <div class="fig__scroll" tabindex="0" role="group" aria-labelledby="fig-5-cap">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 800 135" role="img" aria-labelledby="f5t">
            <title id="f5t">Pipeline of four stages: timing generator, pattern generator, three TMDS encoders and a 10:1 serializer drawn dashed and marked in progress, feeding the TMDS differential outputs. Brackets mark the testbench coverage: the full-frame PPM dump with seven timing counts over the first two stages, and four checks per symbol over the encoder.</title>
            <defs>
              <marker id="arr" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="10" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto"><path d="M0 0 L10 5 L0 10" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"/></marker>
            </defs>
            <rect class="crisp" x="0" y="20" width="140" height="44"/>
            <rect class="crisp" x="190" y="20" width="140" height="44"/>
            <rect class="crisp" x="380" y="20" width="140" height="44"/>
            <rect class="crisp s-ramp" x="570" y="20" width="140" height="44" stroke-dasharray="4 3"/>
            <text class="t-ink" x="70" y="46" text-anchor="middle">timing gen</text>
            <text class="t-ink" x="260" y="46" text-anchor="middle">pattern gen</text>
            <text class="t-ink" x="450" y="46" text-anchor="middle">TMDS enc ×3</text>
            <text class="t-ink" x="640" y="46" text-anchor="middle">10:1 serializer</text>
            <path class="crisp" d="M140 42 H190" marker-end="url(#arr)"/>
            <path class="crisp" d="M330 42 H380" marker-end="url(#arr)"/>
            <path class="crisp" d="M520 42 H570" marker-end="url(#arr)"/>
            <path class="crisp" d="M710 42 H735" marker-end="url(#arr)"/>
            <text class="t-ink" x="742" y="46">TMDS ±</text>
            <text x="0" y="84">25.175 MHz</text>
            <text x="570" y="84">in progress</text>
            <path class="crisp" d="M0 104 H330" stroke-dasharray="4 3"/>
            <path class="crisp" d="M0 104 V98 M330 104 V98"/>
            <text x="0" y="122">TB: full frame → PPM · 7 timing counts</text>
            <path class="crisp" d="M380 104 H520" stroke-dasharray="4 3"/>
            <path class="crisp" d="M380 104 V98 M520 104 V98"/>
            <text x="380" y="122">TB: 4 checks / symbol</text>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <figcaption id="fig-5-cap"><span class="fig__no">Fig.&nbsp;5</span> — Pipeline. Three stages verified in simulation; the 10:1 serializer is being written.</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <h2 class="col-head" id="not-done">What is not done</h2>
      <p class="col-prose">Timing, pattern and encoder are verified in simulation. The <span class="nb">10:1</span> serializer — port list written, body not yet — and board bring-up are in progress. Nothing has been displayed on a monitor, and the page will say so until it has.</p>
      <ul class="check col-prose">
        <li><svg class="chk" viewBox="0 0 10 10" aria-hidden="true"><rect x=".5" y=".5" width="9" height="9"/><path d="M2 5 L4.5 7.5 L8 3"/></svg><span class="check__state">done</span>timing generator</li>
        <li><svg class="chk" viewBox="0 0 10 10" aria-hidden="true"><rect x=".5" y=".5" width="9" height="9"/><path d="M2 5 L4.5 7.5 L8 3"/></svg><span class="check__state">done</span>pattern generator</li>
        <li><svg class="chk" viewBox="0 0 10 10" aria-hidden="true"><rect x=".5" y=".5" width="9" height="9"/><path d="M2 5 L4.5 7.5 L8 3"/></svg><span class="check__state">done</span>TMDS encoder + self-checking testbench</li>
        <li><svg class="chk" viewBox="0 0 10 10" aria-hidden="true"><rect x=".5" y=".5" width="9" height="9"/></svg><span class="check__state">in progress</span>10:1 serializer</li>
        <li><svg class="chk" viewBox="0 0 10 10" aria-hidden="true"><rect x=".5" y=".5" width="9" height="9"/></svg><span class="check__state">in progress</span>board bring-up</li>
      </ul>

    </div>

    <Turn slug={p.slug} />
  </section>

</main>
<script src="../../scripts/tmds.js"></script>
</Base>
